From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 12:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: write the VBIF presets before the firmware boots

preset_limit placed the msm8998 wedge on one write: 0x00000003 to
base+0x80124, the first VBIF register, from venus_set_registers(). Netconsole
carries the marker and the TZ log line and then nothing at all; the phone
returns on the watchdog.

The vendor writes the identical table, but on the other side of the firmware
boot. Downstream __load_fw() is:

	__venus_power_on()	regulators -> clocks -> __set_registers()
	subsystem_get_with_fwname("venus")	<- firmware boots AFTER
	memory protect

mainline is inverted. venus_boot() runs qcom_scm_pas_auth_and_reset() and the
content-protect call first, and venus_set_registers() only runs afterwards out
of hfi_core_resume(). Once TZ has authenticated and reset the block and applied
memory protection, a CPU write into VBIF is no longer obviously ours to make --
which is a coherent reason for one to never return.

presets_early=1 restores the vendor ordering: the presets go in from probe,
immediately before venus_boot(), and venus_run() skips them.

Also worth noting for whoever picks this up: the resume this driver issues at
probe is one the vendor only ever issues when resuming from power collapse
("Reboot the firmware"), never on first boot. TZ answering -EINVAL to it is
therefore expected, and the existing swallow in venus_set_hw_state() is
correct rather than a bug.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c      |  3 +++
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.c | 30 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.h |  1 +
 3 files changed, 33 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 #include "core.h"
 #include "firmware.h"
 #include "pm_helpers.h"
+#include "hfi_venus.h"
 #include "hfi_venus_io.h"
 
 /*
@@ -514,6 +515,9 @@
 	if (venus_stop_before(8))
 		return 0;
 
+	/* Vendor order: the VBIF presets go in before the firmware boots. */
+	venus_hfi_presets_early(core);
+
 	ret = venus_boot(core);
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_firmware_deinit;
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.c
@@ -364,6 +364,31 @@
 	dma_free_attrs(dev, mem->size, mem->kva, mem->da, mem->attrs);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Bring-up bisect, sixth stage -- and the first one taken from the vendor
+ * rather than from bisection.
+ *
+ * preset_limit proved the wedge is the first VBIF write in
+ * venus_set_registers(). The vendor writes the very same table, but on the
+ * other side of the firmware boot. downstream __load_fw() is:
+ *
+ *     __venus_power_on()   regulators -> clocks -> __set_registers()
+ *     subsystem_get_with_fwname("venus")     <- firmware boots AFTER
+ *     memory protect
+ *
+ * mainline is inverted: venus_boot() does qcom_scm_pas_auth_and_reset() and
+ * the CP protect first, and venus_set_registers() only runs later, from
+ * hfi_core_resume(). By then TZ owns the block, which is a coherent reason for
+ * a write into VBIF to never return.
+ *
+ * presets_early=1 restores the vendor order: write the presets from probe,
+ * before venus_boot(), and skip them in venus_run().
+ */
+static int presets_early;
+module_param(presets_early, int, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(presets_early,
+	"write the VBIF register presets before venus_boot(), as downstream does");
+
 static void venus_set_registers(struct venus_hfi_device *hdev)
 {
 	const struct venus_resources *res = hdev->core->res;
@@ -586,7 +611,8 @@
 	if (venus_stop_boot(2))
 		return 0;
 
-	venus_set_registers(hdev);
+	if (!presets_early)
+		venus_set_registers(hdev);
 
 	if (venus_stop_boot(3))
 		return 0;
@@ -1831,3 +1857,11 @@
 
 	mutex_unlock(&hdev->lock);
 }
+
+void venus_hfi_presets_early(struct venus_core *core)
+{
+	struct venus_hfi_device *hdev = to_hfi_priv(core);
+
+	if (presets_early)
+		venus_set_registers(hdev);
+}
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.h b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.h
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_venus.h
@@ -11,5 +11,6 @@
 void venus_hfi_destroy(struct venus_core *core);
 int venus_hfi_create(struct venus_core *core);
 void venus_hfi_queues_reinit(struct venus_core *core);
+void venus_hfi_presets_early(struct venus_core *core);
 
 #endif
